trajectory.patch:
The error log indicates a buffer overflow during the `test_details` test case.
The `strcpy` calls in `test_details` and `test_details_extra` attempt to copy strings like "shell mgmt" (11 bytes with null terminator) into the `expected_name` field of the `details_entries` struct, which is only allocated 4 bytes. This overwrites stack memory and causes the crash.

The fix is to increase the size of the `expected_name` array in the `details_entries` struct to accommodate the longest possible group name.

